# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE ON CONTENT-TYPE — READ BEFORE CHANGING
#
# These .md files are Open Knowledge Format (OKF) documents. Their correct
# media type is text/markdown (RFC 7763), and that is what was served
# originally.
#
# It is deliberately served as text/plain instead, because as of 2026-08
# major agent fetchers REJECT text/markdown:
#   - ChatGPT: "unsupported text/markdown content type" — refuses to fetch
#   - Perplexity: misidentifies it as PDF, fails to parse
# Both were verified by direct test. Under text/markdown the bundle was
# effectively unreachable by the agents it exists to serve.
#
# The bytes are unchanged — markdown IS plain text. What is lost is only the
# media-type signal; the claim that this is markdown is preserved in:
#   - the .md file extension
#   - each file's OKF frontmatter (type:)
#   - the identity node's JSON-LD: "encodingFormat": "text/markdown"
#     (https://companysignet.com/ — subjectOf/Dataset)
#
# INTENT: this SHOULD be text/markdown. Revert to it once agent fetchers
# accept that media type. Re-test before reverting.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

/*.md
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/services/*.md
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
